        <mxCell id="usage" value="Usage rules&#10;&#10;· Cyan always denotes the measured/real side, violet always the simulated/twin side. Keep that mapping consistent across the logo, the UI and any figure in a paper — it lets a reader decode a chart without a legend.&#10;· The mark needs only cyan + slate to be recognisable; violet is what makes it mean &quot;twin&quot;.&#10;· On dark backgrounds swap to the lifted variants (#38BDF8 / #A78BFA); the base hues do not hold enough contrast on #0F172A.&#10;· Never introduce a third accent hue into the mark itself. Additional colours belong to data visualisations only." style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#EFF6FF;strokeColor=#0EA5E9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=16;spacingTop=10;spacingRight=16;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;fontColor=#0F172A;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="340" width="1000" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
